===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sep-}}
{{ubor|en|frm|resipiscence|t=act of recovering one’s senses or coming back to a more acceptable view; repentance}} (modern {{cog|fr|résipiscence}}), or from its {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|LL.|resipīscentia|t=regaining of a clear state of mind, repentance}}, from {{der|en|la|resipīscēns}} + {{m|la|-ia|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|feminine}} {{glossary|abstract noun}}s}}. {{m|la||Resipīscēns}} is the {{glossary|present}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|resipīscō|t=to recover one’s senses; to revive}}, from {{m|la|re-|pos={{glossary|prefix}} meaning ‘again’}} + {{m|la|sapiō|t=to have flavour or taste; (''figurative'') to have good taste or discernment; to be sensible or wise}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*seh₁p-, *sep-|*sep-|to taste; to try out}}) + {{m|la|-īscō}} (a variant of {{m|la|-ēscō|pos=suffix forming {{glossary|adjective}}s with the sense ‘becoming [''something'']’}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=9347758440|date=December 2023}}</ref><ref>{{R:Collins English Dictionary|pos=n}}</ref>

